        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_2303"/>
        <dc:subject>
           <z:AutomaticTag><rdf:value>/unread</rdf:value></z:AutomaticTag>
        </dc:subject>
        <dc:title>OTSun, a python package for the optical analysis of solar-thermal collectors and photovoltaic cells with arbitrary geometry</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Ray tracing software systems are commonly used to analyze the optics of solar energy devices, since they allow to predict the energy gains of devices in real conditions, and also to compare them with other systems constantly emerging in the market. However, the available open-source packages apply excessive simplifications to the model of light-matter interaction, making that the optical behaviour of the systems can not be properly characterized, which in turn implies disagreements between physical experiments and computer simulations. We present here the open source python package OTSun, which applies the Fresnel equations in their most general form, without further simplifications, and is suitable for the simulation of both solar-thermal and photovoltaic systems. The geometrical objects used in this package are created using the parametric 3D modeler FreeCAD, which is also a free and open source program and allows for the construction of arbitrary geometries that can be analyzed with OTSun. These, and other software capabilities, make OTSun extremely flexible and accurate for the optical analysis of solar devices with arbitrary geometry. Additionally, OTSun has a companion webtool, OTSunWebApp, that allows for the usage of certain features of the package without the need to install anything locally. We also show here two numerical experiments that we performed in order to validate the model and implementation: The analysis of the optical efficiency of a Linear Fresnel Reflector (with moving objects), and of a second surface mirror (with variable wavelengths). In each case, the numerical computations had deviations of less than 0.25 percent  from reference models (either computed with another program or with exact formulas).

【摘要翻译】光线跟踪软件系统通常用于分析太阳能器件的光学性能，因为它可以预测器件在实际情况下的能量增益，并与市场上不断出现的其他系统进行比较。然而，现有的开放源码软件包对光-物质相互作用模型进行了过度简化，使得系统的光学行为不能得到适当的描述，这反过来又意味着物理实验和计算机模拟之间的分歧。我们在这里介绍了开源python软件包OTSun，它以最一般的形式应用菲涅耳方程，无需进一步简化，并且适用于光热和光伏系统的模拟。这个软件包中使用的几何对象是使用参数化3D modeler FreeCAD创建的，它也是一个免费开放源代码的程序，允许构造可以用Otsun分析的任意几何形状。这些和其他软件功能使OTSun对于任意几何形状的太阳能器件的光学分析极其灵活和准确。此外，OTSun还有一个配套的webtool，OTSunWebApp，它允许使用包的某些特性，而不需要在本地安装任何东西。为了验证模型和实现，我们还进行了两个数值实验：线性菲涅耳反射器（运动物体）和第二面镜（可变波长）的光学效率分析。在每一种情况下，数值计算与参考模型的偏差都小于0.25%（要么是用另一个程序计算的，要么是用精确的公式计算的）。</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>2020-10-14</dc:date>
        <dc:identifier>
            <dcterms:URI>
                <rdf:value>https://dx.plos.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0240735</rdf:value>
            </dcterms:URI>
        </dc:identifier>
        <dcterms:dateSubmitted>2022-06-25 10:49:19</dcterms:dateSubmitted>
        <dc:coverage>7 citation(s)</dc:coverage>
        <z:shortTitle>OTSun,一个用于任意几何形状的太阳能集热器和 光伏电池光学分析的python软件包</z:shortTitle>
        <z:language>en</z:language>
